{"ld": 1572, "paper": "HP1030", "session": "132", "title": "An Act Regarding Prosecution Standards for Nonfatal Strangulation or Suffocation in Domestic Violence Cases", "sponsor_id": "h-stover-holly", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-gramlich-lori", "h-malon-marc", "h-mastraccio-anne-marie", "h-meyer-michele", "h-moonen-matthew", "s-nangle-timothy", "h-pluecker-william", "s-rotundo-margaret", "h-sayre-daniel"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This bill establishes prosecution standards for nonfatal strangulation or suffocation in domestic assault criminal matters. It:\n\n1. Prohibits the victim, victim's family or victim's dating partner from being able to post bail for the defendant; 2. Allows statements made by the victim during the investigation or preparation for prosecution to be admitted in court without the presence of the victim being required; 3. Prohibits the court from dismissing or allowing unnecessary delay of the disposition of the matter; 4. Prohibits the prosecutor from dismissing, allowing unnecessary delay, deferring or agreeing to a plea of a lesser assault charge; 5. Prohibits a defendant previously convicted of a domestic violence assault charge from entering into a plea agreement; 6. Requires prosecutors, judges, justices, law enforcement officers, defense attorneys and dispatchers to receive training on nonfatal strangulation or suffocation prevention; and 7. Makes domestic violence aggravated assault by means of nonfatal strangulation or suffocation a Class A crime.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1030&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "final_disposition": {"label": "Ought Not to Pass Pursuant To Joint Rule 310", "date": "2026-02-24", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1572)",